WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.770
- [Thoraya] I put up a sign in public

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.050
and it got a lot of attention.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.330
Strangers lined up to
do what the sign said

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.710
and they just kept coming

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.990
because it seemed that
the sign encouraged them

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.410
to do something that they
had already been wanting to.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.330
So what are you here to do today?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.577
- I'm here to let that shit go.

00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:20.130
(interviewee laughing and clapping)

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.960
- Are there any specific instructions

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.793
or do you want me to go ahead

00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:25.140
and start filling out the card?

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.450
- [Thoraya] The first step was to write

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.250
what they wanted to let go of.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.090
- It feels good.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.530
It felt like the right time and place

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.740
to think about something
I wanted to let go of

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:35.820
and let it go.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.590
So it feels cathartic.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.371
- It feels like it's, like,
off my shoulders almost.

00:00:40.371 --> 00:00:41.204
(interviewee grunting)

00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:45.066
- I feel kind of frustrated,
but I'm hoping that changes.

00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:46.170
(interviewee laughing)

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.020
- It feels good, but then
also like, oh, it's silly

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.581
to be mad at something.

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:52.620
(interviewee laughing)

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.950
- I felt kind of like
angry while writing it.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.110
- Doesn't serve me anymore in this life

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.480
so it's nice to write it on a paper

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.330
and kind of let it go in that aspect.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.870
- A little strange to see
it written down on paper.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:11.870
I didn't expect it to be as
impactful as it feels right now.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.113
- It hurts

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.113
a lot.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.800
- I feel relief that someone
else will probably read it

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.350
and I'm hoping to feel
like a whoosh of relief

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.000
once mine is tossed.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.650
I feel calm.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.810
- [Thoraya] Next, they had two options.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.710
They could either get rid of
the piece of paper themselves

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.770
or they could leave it for
another stranger to read.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.210
- I want someone else to read it.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.216
- I'll leave it to someone else.

00:01:41.216 --> 00:01:42.360
- And I just read it out loud?

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.180
- [Thoraya] And instruct
them on how to get rid of it.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.950
- And then on the back it
says, "Rip up those feelings

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.000
and toss them away."

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.833
- Toss it.

00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:50.880
- Tear this shit up please.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.170
- Tear it up then burn it.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.985
- Crumple it and toss.

00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:54.818
Okay.

00:01:54.818 --> 00:01:55.680
- Aw, this one says nurture it.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.840
So I'm gonna go ahead and
do that, I'm gonna do that.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.920
- I have to kiss it first

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.300
and then I have to burn it in a bonfire.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.100
So I have to take it back
with me so I can burn it.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.823
- Give this card a kiss and just toss it.

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:07.380
(lips smacking)

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.520
- [Thoraya] And once they were done,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.040
I asked them to read a
note that another stranger

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.030
was kind enough to not only
share with them, but all of you.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.280
- Ooh, I feel this.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.404
- Wow, that's crazy.

00:02:20.404 --> 00:02:21.960
It's something I really relate to.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:22.793
- Oh, man.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.503
- Okay, just read it?

00:02:24.503 --> 00:02:25.860
- Should I read it out loud?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.870
- This person said, "I hate my body.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.430
I wish I could learn to appreciate

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.030
and accept that part of me,
but I am very shameful."

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.440
We gotta let that shit go.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.882
We gotta let that shit go.

00:02:35.882 --> 00:02:38.290
(interviewee laughing)

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.080
- "I would like to let go
of the resentment I have

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.647
towards people who have hurt
me for no reason in the past."

00:02:45.725 --> 00:02:47.527
(interviewee murmurs)

00:02:47.527 --> 00:02:50.640
- "I can't talk to people I don't know.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.490
My words get mixed up in my head

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.167
and I can't breathe normally."

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:57.408
(interviewee exhales)

00:02:57.408 --> 00:02:59.670
I think a lot of people feel this way

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.510
and a lot of times, we're so
focused on our experience,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.150
but other people are not even noticing

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.560
that we're having a hard time.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.680
Just trying to remember
that they're not alone.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.237
That's kind of part of
the human experience.

00:03:13.237 --> 00:03:17.040
- "I'm trying to be more me
and less who you think I am.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.920
I don't know why
expectations and perceptions

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.477
have so much power over me."

00:03:23.587 --> 00:03:25.027
- "Hateful feelings."

00:03:25.027 --> 00:03:27.517
- "My anger towards people."

00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:30.037
- "Wanna let go of small town negativity."

00:03:30.037 --> 00:03:34.050
- "I am still not sure that
I understand forgiveness."

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.460
I'm with them.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.760
I'm right there with them.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.620
I don't know if any of us
truly understand forgiveness.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.930
I think that our understanding of that

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.020
will change as the years go on.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.110
And as we continue to inflict pain

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.960
onto other people and
experience it ourselves.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.760
I think it'll continue to change.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.773
Definition of forgiveness right now?

00:03:57.457 --> 00:03:59.040
(interviewee exhaling)

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.310
Being able to not necessarily empathize

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.620
with what someone has done to you,

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.500
but sympathize with
what they've done to you

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.500
and accept it instead of actually
understanding how or why,

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.353
accepting that they did.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.410
- I'm not ready to let go of anything yet

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.410
because I'm still learning from it.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.713
And I'll release it
when I'm done learning.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.610
- Ooh, I feel this.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.590
It says, "Procrastination.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.600
I haven't done my taxes."

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.767
I gotta do mine, too, I feel that.

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.500
- "The pressure of being expected

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.470
to be immediately successful
as a young adult."

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.480
Woo, I understand that.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.740
I am not really a young adult,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.957
but I understand self-imposed
pressure to be successful.

00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:53.460
- "Grief that piles up and
makes me feel too heavy

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.720
to be confident.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:55.597
Self-doubt."

00:04:55.597 --> 00:04:58.237
- "My obsession of being normal."

00:04:58.237 --> 00:05:00.307
- "Refusing to take care of myself."

00:05:00.307 --> 00:05:03.510
- "I have been sensitive
for way too long."

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.710
Well, this person who wrote
this is working on it.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:10.560
And I would say to keep going
and keep talking about it

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.987
and keep working on it and
explore it a little bit more.

00:05:13.987 --> 00:05:15.960
- "I found so much freedom and power

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.417
in realizing that I don't have to."

00:05:20.856 --> 00:05:22.779
I really like this one

00:05:22.779 --> 00:05:23.612
(interviewee laughing)

00:05:23.612 --> 00:05:27.330
because it kind of matches what I wrote

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:31.147
and it makes me feel
better after what I wrote.

00:05:31.147 --> 00:05:33.750
- "I still check what music she listens to

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.477
and wonder if her playlists are about me."

00:05:37.731 --> 00:05:39.097
- "My feelings for my ex."

00:05:39.097 --> 00:05:42.180
- "I can't forget about my
ex who treated me horribly.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.890
She's moved on, but I still love her

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.450
and I want to let it go.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.470
It's been eight months

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.660
and she's the only girl I've ever loved."

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.474
I had a feeling I would
get something like this.

00:05:50.474 --> 00:05:51.307
(interviewee laughing)

00:05:51.307 --> 00:05:54.720
- "The anger I still have towards my ex."

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.070
I guess he broke her heart.

00:05:57.029 --> 00:05:58.830
So, but they ain't telling
me to do nothin' with it,

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.321
so I guess they want me to go find them.

00:06:02.321 --> 00:06:05.214
(interviewee laughing)

00:06:05.214 --> 00:06:07.587
You just can't just give
somebody your heart like that.

00:06:07.587 --> 00:06:09.060
I mean, you should just,
like, slice his tires

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.810
or something like that cause
I like 'em crazy, you dig?

00:06:12.658 --> 00:06:13.740
(interviewee laughing)

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.390
I want my girl to slice my tires.

00:06:16.405 --> 00:06:17.347
(interviewee laughing)

00:06:17.347 --> 00:06:19.537
- "Longing for someone I've never met."

00:06:19.537 --> 00:06:22.770
- "The constant desire to meet my person."

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.060
I kind of love that 'cause I feel like

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.340
there's so much pressure nowadays

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.270
to, like, meet the right person.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.620
Like, that you have a soulmate out there

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.300
that you, like, are gonna
meet at the right place

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.133
at the right time.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:32.880
And so you're always, like, stressed about

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.890
when that's gonna be and
like how to set yourself up

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.920
for that and so I think it's
awesome to, like, let that go

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.630
and just be yourself and
that person will come to you

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.300
eventually if there is
that kind of person.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.459
- Wow, that's crazy.

00:06:45.459 --> 00:06:46.867
It's something I really relate to.

00:06:46.867 --> 00:06:50.400
"Feeling confused about if
my mother was there for me

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.410
the way I needed her to be

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.270
and loving her so much still."

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.790
And it said, "I want you to burn this."

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:01.790
So I will burn this for them
as a good community member.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.960
- They said, "My mom."

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.630
- This person put, "I really want kids,

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.650
but I'll never admit it

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.717
as I think I'd turn out like my mom."

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.600
I feel that

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.570
- I wrote, "Disappointment
and expectations

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.037
from my parents."

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.500
Can I read one?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:24.420
Having to leave my parents to
chase different opportunities.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.380
Whoa, that's kind of weird.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.420
Ours were kind of like the opposite.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.819
That's so weird.

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:31.736
Okay, I didn't like it.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:36.000
- So I wrote "Anger,
resentment, and frustration

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:36.833
towards my father."

00:07:36.833 --> 00:07:39.360
He wasn't very kind in my childhood.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.022
And he's gotten better,
he's gotten better.

00:07:43.022 --> 00:07:46.412
But it's still not a hundred
percent and that hurts.

00:07:46.412 --> 00:07:47.820
But let's see somebody else's shit

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:48.750
that we're about to let out.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:49.920
Let's see.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.327
Ah, see, like, same shit, same shit.

00:07:52.327 --> 00:07:54.090
"The amount of guilt I
feel when thinking about

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:56.580
how critical I've been to my parents."

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.883
No, yeah, I totally agree.

00:07:58.883 --> 00:07:59.880
I think that like when
things get heated, you know,

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:01.470
people say things that
they don't really mean

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:04.950
and it's not a good, like, family dynamic.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.490
Then you grow up and you learn
all these, like, bad lessons

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:09.810
on, like, how you should treat people

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:13.530
and, like, the feelings you
have towards other people

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.730
and, like, what they did.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.157
At the end of the day, no
one's perfect, you know?

00:08:17.157 --> 00:08:20.070
And it's not healthy for
you to be holding out

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.170
all that bad negative energy.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:24.470
It's just, you know,
like, you only live once.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.740
So, like, why spend it
miserably, you know?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.677
It's just no point.

00:08:29.677 --> 00:08:34.170
- "Expectations placed on me
by my religious community.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:36.870
I want to express myself and be me

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.990
rather than be what I am expected to be."

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.290
- This one says, "Negative
feelings towards myself."

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.120
Something we all struggle with

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.857
that we all are here
to learn and overcome.

00:08:47.857 --> 00:08:49.170
- "I am so mad at (no audio)

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.750
for not responding to my
email and text message.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.067
She at least should be
considerate of my time."

00:08:54.067 --> 00:08:57.300
- "I want to get rid of being
unemployed and video games

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.027
so that I can care for
my wife in a deep way."

00:09:01.027 --> 00:09:03.840
- "I navigate the world
as if every word I say

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.130
can be used against me.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.617
I'm not even sure who I
am, so mistrusting of."

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.110
I can most definitely relate to it.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.903
It's essentially similar
to what I wrote myself.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:17.700
- And then this one says,
"I've never told anyone this,

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.140
because I don't like upsetting anyone

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.540
from how morbid it sounds.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.280
But I think about s****de every day.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.860
It's exhausting and I just
wish it felt more comfortable

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.910
talking about it."

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:28.980
Well, I hope that person is listening

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.290
and I hope that they are more
comfortable speaking about it

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.060
and they don't think about that any longer

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.060
because, I mean, they don't
deserve to feel that way.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:38.460
So I'm really hoping
that they let that go.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.367
And they said, "Give this
card a kiss and just toss it."

00:09:43.045 --> 00:09:43.878
Okay.

00:09:43.878 --> 00:09:44.711
(lips smacking)

00:09:44.711 --> 00:09:47.294
(gentle music)

